<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucala River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lukala River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lucala River is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> and the largest tributary of the Kwanza, which it joins near Massangano. The lands between the Lucala and the Kwanza formed the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbundu">Mbundu</a> kingdom of Ndongo, and the Portuguese built forts along its course during their wars of conquest in the 16th and 17th centuries. The Kalandula Falls lie on the river.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucala-river.jpg" alt="Lucala River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: L.Willms · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quedas-Kalandula_11_escoa-o-rio-Lucala_LWS-2011-08_QD36.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
